Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and I (mostly Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81) were sick =
for the past week, mega zest (as
Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 would say). There are a few positives though! (The=
re always are
baby =F0=9F=94=A5)

This week we had =E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=E5=A4=A7=E4=BC=9A (chouroutaikai) aka E=
lders Conference. Unfortunately
we didn't get to meet mission wide, but we did get to gather in our
respective zones. We basically played random sports, Pok=C3=A9mon, and Beyb=
lades
in the Takamatsu church building (I spent most of the time playing
Pok=C3=A9mon).

It was super fun to see Wheeler=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and Dietrich=E9=95=B7=E8=
=80=81, I've yet to bump into
Fair=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 yet however=F0=9F=98=A2. It'll happen sometime soon =
I'm sure.

This week was a tough one for me personally. It feels hard to use my time
effectively locked inside the apartment when my Companion is getting some
Z's. I've had a lot of time to reflect on how I'm using my time, which is a
good thing! One thing I learned is that it's pretty easy to let yourself
get lured into laziness when you have an excuse for it. I think that there
are definitely times where a break for peace of mind is warranted, but all
too often we ride those excuses and end up wasting our time or using it
much less effectively than we could be. This is a pretty hard
feeling/mindset to combat from my experience. It is, however, possible! If
we jump up, and make up our minds to do something more, the energy starts
flowing and stuff gets done. That first step is never very easy,
Unfortunately.

"Breaking out" is something I could definitely use some work on. I think
that a couple ways I've "broken out" is by getting sick of using time a
certain way (definitely not the ideal method) or by relying on others to
hold me accountable and help to motivate me (IDEAL!! =F0=9F=94=A5).

I really don't believe that we will be stuck in a negative mindset/way of
life  forever, (most of the time we eventually move on) but it can take a
really really long time to change on your own. My invitation is to try and
rely on someone else to improve some aspect of your life. Sometimes we feel
like "oh, I don't want to burden this person" or even "I can do it by
myself." These statements have some elements of truth; relying on others
does take some amount of effort from the other person, and you probably
could do things on your own. BUT! More often than not it is pretty
ineffective trying to manage it all yourself. People are usually pretty
willing to help you out too! =F0=9F=98=81

I know that as we turn outwards (for help or to provide help) we will find
light in our lives. I have felt Christ's light in my life, and that's
definitely part of why I'm out spending 2 years of my life trying to share
that with people! I encourage you to share your light, and sometimes to let
other's light shine on you =F0=9F=98=84

"Verily, verily, I say unto you, I give unto you to be the light of this
people."

-Jesus Christ

(From 3 Nephi 12:14)

Love you guys, each and every one of you! I'd love to hear from you too!
Let me know what's up! =F0=9F=98=81

=E3=82=AD=E3=83=AA=E3=82=A2=E3=83=B3=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81

